# Profiling slot-template (feature 002 + 009: contracts/scenario-row.md). Performance rows use the
# single neutral voice persona (steady-caller). Judge-graded rows (degradation, barge-in,
# consistency) go in the perf-* banks; latency/error-rate probes are measured by the .py code
# checks. Keep run-parameter-distinct probes as their own eval_config entries (FR-002).
# Feature 009: state the correct outcome ONCE, in `result` (scenario_result). NEVER put an
# `expected_behavior` (or any answer-key text) inside `input` — it would leak to the simulated
# caller and validation now rejects it.
{"input": {"sub_capability": "{sub_capability}", "persona": "{caller_demeanor}", "script": "{behavioral_arc_directives}", "severity_on_fail": "Medium"}, "result": "{pass_criterion_ie_what_the_agent_should_do}"}
